---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Micro Instrument Repair
permalink: /repair-services/micro-instrument-repair/
---
{# Repair - Micro Instrument (Figma 35098:38988, the client's 1600px frame on the WIP page); the URL is the live
   site's. No redesigned or phone frame exists, so the sections use the redesign's components and type scale:
   - Hero: the shared content hero with the frame's photo and fade, the title, the frame's intro (drawn under the
     hero in Figma) and the "Download Repair Form" button.
   - "Typical Repair Charges": the frame's four price tables (navy header, rows alternating white and #f5f8fa), as
     real tables. Every cell border is the same light outline, including the line before the price column that Figma
     draws navy, and the tables get the 4px corners.
   - "Request a Repair" under the prices (not in the frame): the strip of Figma's "Request a Free Repair"
     (35122:1338, its header row without the steps), so the repair form is offered again once the prices are read.
   - Free Lifetime Repair band: the PLP banner (34777:59015), the same seal, copy and button.
   - "SEO Text": the PLP features list (bold lead-in, orange dashes).
   - FAQ: the shared FAQ section; it loads closed (Figma's orange question is a hover example) and the answers
     are the live page's. #}
{% import "macros/ui.njk" as ui with context %}
{% import "content/macros.njk" as c with context %}
{% import "plp/macros.njk" as plp_ui with context %}
{% set m = contentPages.micro %}

{{ ui.breadcrumbs([{ label: "Repair Services", href: "/repair-services/" }, { label: "Micro Instrument" }]) }}

{# Hero: the instruments photo (a cut-out on white) on the right under the frame's navy fade (microFade). Figma's photo
   is 124% of the hero's height, 3px from the top and 1.6% past the right edge; on narrower screens it slides further
   out so it never starts left of the 593px text column; past 1920px it keeps its 1920 place beside the centred content
   (right edge at 50% + 991px), with white beyond it. The intro is longer than on the other heroes, so the hero grows
   past its 480px (the photo still reaches the bottom from lg; below lg it ends on white). Phones: navy behind the photo, which sits on the right under
   a 60% navy tint so the white title stays readable over the light instruments. #}
{% call c.hero({
  title: "Micro / Ophthalmic Instrument Repair", text: m.intro, figma: "35098:39055", image: "d61fe469",
  bg: "bg-primary-500 md:bg-white", fade: contentPages.gradients.microFade,
  photo: "right-[-20%] top-0 h-full w-auto max-w-none md:right-[min(-1.6%,calc(100%_-_1183px))] md:top-[3px] md:h-[446px] md:w-[558px] lg:right-[max(min(-1.6%,calc(100%_-_1372px)),calc(50%_-_991px))] lg:h-[597px] lg:w-[747px]",
  scrim: "bg-primary-500/60 md:hidden"
}) %}
  {{ c.arrowButton("Download Repair Form", "#", "data-proto", "w-full md:w-auto") }}
{% endcall %}

{# Typical Repair Charges ("Content" 35098:39067, the intro moved into the hero): 36px between the title and the tables.
   The request strip follows 60px under the last table (36px gap + 24px): #f1f5f8, 24/32 padding, the 32px navy tool
   icon, Bold 18/28 title over a 16/24 line, the primary download button on the right. Phones: icon and text in a row,
   the button full width under them.
   Tables: Medium 24/32 white header (Bold service name), Regular 18/28 navy rows 64px tall with their 1px bottom line,
   Bold prices in a 300px column. Phones: 20/28 header, 16/24 rows, 112px price column; names may break after a "/". #}
<section class="bg-white" aria-labelledby="charges-title" data-figma="35098:39067">
  <div class="container-page flex flex-col gap-6 py-10 md:gap-9 md:py-[50px]">
    <h2 id="charges-title" class="text-h3 font-medium text-heading md:text-h2 md:font-bold lg:text-h1" data-figma="35098:39069">Typical Repair Charges</h2>
    {% for box in m.charges %}
    <table class="w-full table-fixed border-separate border-spacing-0 text-left" data-figma="{{ box.figma }}">
      <colgroup><col><col class="w-28 md:w-[300px]"></colgroup>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th colspan="2" scope="colgroup" class="rounded-t bg-primary-500 px-4 py-3 text-h4 font-normal text-white md:py-4 md:text-h3"><span class="font-bold">{{ box.name }}</span> - {{ box.work }}</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="text-base text-primary-500 md:text-lg">
        {% for row in box.rows %}
        {% set tint = "bg-menu" if loop.index % 2 == 0 else "bg-white" %}
        <tr>
          <th scope="row" class="{{ tint }} {{ 'rounded-bl' if loop.last }} border-b border-l border-outline px-4 pb-[11px] pt-3 font-normal md:pb-[17px] md:pt-[18px]">{{ row[0] | escape | replace("/", "/<wbr>") | safe }}</th>
          <td class="{{ tint }} {{ 'rounded-br' if loop.last }} border-b border-l border-r border-outline px-4 pb-[11px] pt-3 font-bold md:pb-[17px] md:pt-[18px]">{{ row[1] | money }}</td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    {% endfor %}
    <section id="request-repair" aria-labelledby="request-title" class="mt-4 flex flex-col gap-4 rounded bg-secondary-100 px-5 py-6 md:mt-6 md:flex-row md:items-center md:gap-6 md:px-8" data-figma="35122:1338">
      <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 items-center gap-4 md:gap-6" data-figma="35176:927">
        {% icon "tool", "h-8 w-8 text-primary-500" %}
        <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
          <h2 id="request-title" class="text-lg font-bold text-heading">Request a Repair</h2>
          <p class="text-base text-body">No RMA number needed.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <a href="#" data-proto class="btn-primary w-full shrink-0 whitespace-nowrap pr-[30px] md:w-auto" data-figma="35122:1344">Download Repair Form{% icon "download" %}</a>
    </section>
  </div>
</section>

{{ plp_ui.repairBanner() }}

<div class="pb-8 md:pb-10">{{ plp_ui.features(m.seo) }}</div>

{{ c.faqSection(m.faq, { section: "35098:39179", list: "35098:39182", card: "34799:68654" }) }}
